    <values><field>CheckTitle__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Refused: BeyondQueryLimit</value></values>
    <values><field>CheckDescription__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Row 3 of a query that ends in LIMIT 1. The query's own ceiling is tighter than the Check's, and the row can never exist. Deliberately misconfigured and deployed anyway, so the refusal is proven.</value></values>
    <values><field>EvaluationType__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >QUERY</value></values>
    <values><field>SourceQuery__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >SELECT Id, LastName FROM Contact WHERE AccountId = {!record.Id} ORDER BY Id LIMIT 1</value></values>
    <values><field>SourceQueryField__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Id</value></values>
    <values><field>QueryResultHandling__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >ALL_ROWS_PASS</value></values>
    <values><field>ComparisonOperator__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >IS_NOT_BLANK</value></values>
    <values><field>FailureMessage__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Third contact is {!rhcQuery.sourceRows[3].LastName}.</value></values>
    <values><field>FailureSeverity__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >INFO</value></values>
    <values><field>UnableToEvaluateMessage__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >This Check is misconfigured and was not evaluated.</value></values>
